1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,396
The Best Part Was Tiny.

3
00:00:03,396 --> 00:00:06,448
At dinner on Sunday, Mom asks us a question.

4
00:00:06,448 --> 00:00:08,875
She wants to know one good thing from the week.

5
00:00:08,875 --> 00:00:12,510
Ben immediately says dessert, even though dessert hasn't happened yet.

6
00:00:12,772 --> 00:00:15,234
Something that already happened, please.

7
00:00:15,234 --> 00:00:17,557
Lucy, what was your favorite part?

8
00:00:17,836 --> 00:00:19,684
Mine was something small.

9
00:00:19,684 --> 00:00:22,955
Emma saved me a seat at lunch on a day when I felt tired.

10
00:00:22,955 --> 00:00:24,976
She didn't make a big deal of it.

11
00:00:24,976 --> 00:00:27,548
She just moved her backpack and smiled.

12
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,770
That sounds like a good day.

13
00:00:30,004 --> 00:00:31,654
It became a better day.

14
00:00:31,654 --> 00:00:32,987
What about you?

15
00:00:33,268 --> 00:00:35,855
I found the screwdriver I'd been looking for.

16
00:00:35,855 --> 00:00:38,439
It was exactly where I had put it away.

17
00:00:38,716 --> 00:00:40,001
Amazing.

18
00:00:40,001 --> 00:00:42,085
A mystery with no mystery.

19
00:00:42,364 --> 00:00:46,066
My favorite moment was hearing you two laugh while you folded the laundry.

20
00:00:46,066 --> 00:00:48,295
I almost didn't want to interrupt.

21
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:50,897
That was the missing-sock investigation.

22
00:00:50,897 --> 00:00:53,042
A very serious operation.

23
00:00:53,042 --> 00:00:56,313
Ben thinks for a moment, then looks toward the kitchen window.

24
00:00:56,596 --> 00:00:58,746
Professor Leaf has a new leaf.

25
00:00:58,746 --> 00:01:00,642
I noticed it this morning.

26
00:01:00,916 --> 00:01:02,024
Really?

27
00:01:02,024 --> 00:01:04,160
You'll have to show us after dinner.

28
00:01:04,444 --> 00:01:07,313
We all turn to look at the little plant in its yellow pot.

29
00:01:07,313 --> 00:01:10,709
Ben stands up proudly, as if he grew the leaf himself.

30
00:01:10,709 --> 00:01:14,115
I realize nobody chose anything expensive or enormous.

31
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:17,229
A seat, a tool, a laugh, a leaf.

32
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,575
Now, who would like dessert?

33
00:01:19,804 --> 00:01:21,048
Finally.

34
00:01:21,048 --> 00:01:23,475
My next favorite moment is arriving.

35
00:01:23,764 --> 00:01:25,685
We pass the plates around.

36
00:01:25,685 --> 00:01:27,779
I decide I like this game.

37
00:01:27,779 --> 00:01:33,258
Next week, I'll pay a little more attention to the tiny good things, especially the ones that happen before dessert.
